 "result": "Based on the subagent's report, two failing tests are not caused by the `partitioned` kwarg, plus one flaky test whose cause wasn't confirmed:\n\n1. **`test_request.py::test_limit_config`**: it expects `max_form_memory_size` to default to `500_000` when no app is active (`wrappers.py:110-111`). Werkzeug 3.0.3 returns `None`, because that default came in with Werkzeug 3.1. It is a separate symptom of the same installed-version mismatch, not the `set_cookie` problem.\n\n2. **`test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view`**: `asgiref` isn't installed, so `app.py:1096` (`async_to_sync`) raises `RuntimeError: Install Tessel with the 'async' extra...`. This is a missing optional dependency, unrelated to Werkzeug.\n\n3. **`test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]`** (flaky, unconfirmed): it failed only in the full run and passed when run alone. The subagent suspects it is contaminated by the leaked generator from `test_stream_keeps_session`, which would make it indirectly caused by the main root cause. It never read this test's traceback, so I can't state a cause with confidence.",
